  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Validating a franchise model to provide Indian lower middle class with healthy and affordable meals</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In India the growth of the lower middle classes has led to an increasing number of people suffering from overweight and obesities, mostly in informal settlements and slumps. People have little knowledge of health, hygiene and good quality nutritious food and are being confronted with cheap and unhealthy snacks everywhere. For various reasons people have no access to good quality, healthy and nutritious food.  People&#x2019;s Meals is a Dutch social entrepreneurial business venture in Delhi, India, locally active under the name of Homeals.  The company aims to make low cost high quality and healthy meals available to large numbers of people. Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) provided support to validate the commercial viability of the model and to prepare for future scale-up investments. The project included the upscaling of the central kitchen and standardising cooking processes to prepare meals, set-up a cold-distribution network and the set-up of a replicable franchise model to eventually produce and serve 10,000 meals per day each.  The project supported 14 direct jobs, 16 indirect jobs, provided on the job training and knowledge transfer to 14 people and has led to Food Safety and Security Certification in India. Currently, the franchise model is still  under development after which the company is hopeful to be able to raise further investments to upscale and replicate the model across North-India.</narrative>
  </description>
